      "title": "Error-detecting codes run real arithmetic on a trapped-ion computer",
      "summary": "Researchers ran ripple-carry addition circuits on inputs of up to five bits on Quantinuum's Helios-1 trapped-ion computer. They used error-detecting codes and report running below the threshold at which the protection starts to pay off. This is an early demonstration of fault-tolerant design on real hardware, but the circuits are tiny and far from the scale useful problems need.",
